{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "AngleNestedFields",
    "description": "esm-spec \u00a74.8.3 'And an angle is CONVERTED', in the expression-bearing fields beyond `args`: a circular-trig argument in `deg` is brought to radians wherever the call sits, including a `makearray` region value and a `table_lookup` axis input. With latitude = 30 deg, `v` integrates dv/dt = [sin 30, cos 30, cos 30] = [0.5, sqrt(3)/2, sqrt(3)/2] to t = 1, and `tl` = T(sin 30) with T(x) = 10 x on [0, 1], so 5. Rust's rewrite used to descend only into `args`, `lower`, `upper` and `expr`, so these reached its evaluator in degrees: sin(30 rad) = -0.988. Sibling of angle_array_element.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "scalar_operator_semantics",
      "inline-test",
      "units",
      "angle",
      "esm-spec-4.8.3"
    ],
    "license": "MIT"
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    }
  },
  "function_tables": {
    "T": {
      "description": "T(x) = 10 x on [0, 1].",
      "axes": [
        {
          "name": "x",
          "values": [
            0.0,
            1.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "interpolation": "linear",
      "out_of_bounds": "clamp",
      "data": [
        0.0,
        10.0
      ]
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "AngleNestedFields": {
      "variables": {
        "latitude": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 30.0,
          "description": "A latitude in DEGREES."
        },
        "tl": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "A `table_lookup` whose axis input is sin(latitude): 10 sin 30 = 5."
        },
        "probe": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Integrates `tl`, so the value is read as well as computed."
        },
        "v": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "cells"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Integrates a `makearray` whose region values are sin and cos of `latitude`: dv/dt = [0.5, sqrt(3)/2, sqrt(3)/2], so v(1) is that array."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "v"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "makearray",
            "args": [],
            "regions": [
              [
                [
                  1,
                  1
                ]
              ],
              [
                [
                  2,
                  3
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "values": [
              {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  "latitude"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  "latitude"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tl",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "table_lookup",
            "table": "T",
            "axes": {
              "x": {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  "latitude"
                ]
              }
            },
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "probe"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": "tl"
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "angle_nested_fields_values",
          "description": "Each degree-valued argument reaches its circular function in RADIANS: inside a makearray region value (read through the state it drives, so the right-hand side evaluates it) and inside a table_lookup axis input (a build-time observed). Unconverted, sin(30 rad) = -0.988. The band on `v` allows for the integrator over a constant derivative.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 1.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1e-10,
            "abs": 1e-12
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "v",
              "time": 1.0,
              "expected": 0.5,
              "coords": {
                "cells": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "v",
              "time": 1.0,
              "expected": 0.8660254037844386,
              "coords": {
                "cells": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "v",
              "time": 1.0,
              "expected": 0.8660254037844386,
              "coords": {
                "cells": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "tl",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 5.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
